    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0324" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1964</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Russell to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-11T15:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 11, 1916, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Arrived this morning, everything quiet.</p>
                <p>Your December 9, 6 p.m. Dominican Minister for Foreign Affairs telegraphed
                    Dominican Minister at Washington November 30 to protest officially to Department
                    of State and foreign missions action American Government.</p>
                <p>Captain Knapp has placed officers in various departments to transact official
                    business.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
